From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:54:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Guard: teleports keep the client's motion and onGround; drop
 the world reference

From enforcing on sg1: players held on match pedestals were set back again
and again. A position the server sends leaves the client's motion and its
onGround as they were, so after a teleport:
- the first move is seeded as on the ground, with an ordinary block's grip,
  and the motion carried from before (horizontal and vertical);
- a move dropped by CraftBukkit's justTeleported check resets the guard;
- the first checked move may rise on the vertical speed it carried, and may
  end floating against a wall met on the way down.

A box rebuilt from its centre (a teleport, a setback) can overlap a block it
touches by 1e-15 and stand on its edge or bump its head on it. The ground,
landing and ceiling probes now accept a block the box only touches when its
top is at the feet (not a wall that goes on above) or its bottom at the head;
a multi-tick landing may step up onto such an edge before jumping. The
ground probe's tolerance is 1e-5 instead of 0.001, which counted a client
0.0008 over a block as standing on it.

AthenaGuardMovementTest gains a run that teleports the client back to where
it was a few ticks before, sometimes 0.01 above it; 18 seeds x 3000 runs of
both honest tests are clean.

The guard also held the World of the last move it checked, for its log line:
a player standing still kept an unloaded match world alive. sg1 ran out of
its 144 MB heap loading the eighth match world in seventeen minutes with an
idle player on; the reference is now dropped after each check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

